WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 073. ACCESS FOR WHOM?. A celebratory reform signal is only the first layer. Legal change is not the same as usable access.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
ADD THE CONSTRAINTS. COST · GEOGRAPHY · ELIGIBILITY · LEGAL RISK. Practical access changes when the route, price, rules, workforce, and uncertainty remain visible.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
ASK WHO IS EXCLUDED. DISABILITY · LANGUAGE · CULTURE · WORKFORCE. Eight indicators stay separate so one favorable signal cannot erase another barrier.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
SHOW THE METHOD. NO WEIGHTING · RANKING · CERTIFICATION. The index preserves descriptive signals and unknowns without manufacturing a composite equity score.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. A MAP CANNOT DETERMINE ACCESS OR EQUITY. Synthetic contexts only; no protected-trait inference, current-law, eligibility, clinical, safety, cultural-authority, consent, or representativeness claim.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. ASK WHO CAN ACTUALLY USE THE SERVICE. ACCESS INTELLIGENCE BEGINS WHEN REFORM, COST, PLACE, ELIGIBILITY, CULTURE, DISABILITY, LANGUAGE, WORKFORCE, LEGAL RISK, AND UNKNOWNS STAY VISIBLE.

